cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HandoverLab: system-level simulation of handover and mobility beyond 5G"
abstract: >-
  HandoverLab is an open-source, system-level simulator of 3GPP Release-16 mobility procedures
  (baseline handover with Event A3, and conditional handover) for many users in dense 5G and
  beyond-5G networks. It provides a TR 38.901 received-power radio model, an L3-filtered
  measurement chain, a radio-link failure model, an outcome label for every handover attempt,
  a plug-in interface for handover rules, equal-budget tuning studies with paired statistics,
  and verification against hand-computed values, golden event-log fingerprints and ns-3 / 5G-LENA.
version: "1.0.0rc1"
date-released: 2026-10-15
